00:11:48.124 --> 00:11:49.290
So I'm going to talk to you.

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:51.140
We've each got 10
minutes, and I'm

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:55.100
going to try and really give
you a snapshot of the work we've

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:59.270
been doing with Google on the
Partner Cloud Interconnect.

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:01.490
We've been working with
Google for several years

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:06.470
now, even back to
Layer 3 peering.

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:09.260
And so it's just been a
wonderful relationship,

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:12.110
and it's come quite a long way.

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:14.810
So I'm going to introduce you to
ECX, which is the Equinix Cloud

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:15.410
Exchange.

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:17.540
And it really started as
Equinix Cloud Exchange

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:21.000
and only recently
became the Fabric.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:24.110
This Cloud Exchange
started as a way,

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:27.860
really, to offer
efficient connectivity

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:32.030
for customers like Google
to multiple enterprises.

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:34.190
And you can see the
features are it's on demand,

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:38.090
it's private networking, it's
private network connectivity.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:40.990
It's completely software
defined and API enabled,

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:42.690
and I'll show you
that in a minute.

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.590
And it's available
in 30-plus metros.

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:48.904
So we're in 52 metros around
the world, and Google's with us

00:12:48.904 --> 00:12:49.460
in 21.

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:51.110
Well, with the launch
of Fabric, which

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:56.480
really is us interconnecting
our data centers together,

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:58.850
we've now extended
the reach with Google

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:00.230
to an additional 10 metros.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:02.660
So it's 31 altogether.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:05.420
And so you can get
multiple connection options

00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:06.470
to Google Cloud.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:08.780
You can do private
direct connect,

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:13.010
or you can do it over the
Cloud Exchange Fabric.

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:15.450
You also, though, can connect
to your own infrastructure.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:17.990
So if you're in multiple
sites, you actually

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:22.530
can connect to yourself
across those metros,

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:25.520
and whether that's for
primary DR, et cetera,

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:27.680
or finding somebody else
within the ecosystem

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:28.910
that you want to connect to.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.290
And that's really,
in a nutshell,

00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:33.170
what Cloud Exchange is.

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:36.031
So where the Google Partner
Interconnect is located

00:13:36.031 --> 00:13:36.530
is here.

00:13:36.530 --> 00:13:39.350
You can see the
multiple locations.

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:47.030
These are the 21 if you overlay
where the Interconnect exists.

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:51.170
And then the Fabric is how we've
connected our sites together.

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:55.470
We're live in both
the US and EMEA.

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:57.650
We'll be live in
the next few weeks

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:02.060
interconnecting our data centers
in Asia, so APAC will go live.

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:04.220
As you can see, it's
dotted because it's

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:07.370
